00:17:24.576 --> 00:17:26.845 align:start size:56% position:44%
So, this weighs
106 kilograms,

00:17:26.878 --> 00:17:28.480 align:start size:63% position:38%
which is 230 pounds.

00:17:28.513 --> 00:17:30.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Metric system. I like it.
- Yes.

00:17:30.748 --> 00:17:32.417 size:88% position:56%
And to fly the same distance

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:35.454 align:start size:75% position:25%
in a gasoline-powered
version of that plane...

00:17:35.487 --> 00:17:40.325 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Mm-hmm.
- ...the fuel weighs
  just this much.

00:17:40.358 --> 00:17:42.694 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Whoa.
- So, when people say
  that fossil fuels

00:17:42.727 --> 00:17:45.497 align:start size:75% position:25%
are really energy dense,
this is what they're
talking about.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.432 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Hmm.
- So, this difference

00:17:47.465 --> 00:17:49.835 align:start size:97% position:3%
becomes really challenging
when you move to bigger planes.

00:17:49.868 --> 00:17:52.337 align:start position:0%
Yeah, I bet.
Oh, that one's huge.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:55.674 align:start size:66% position:34%
( laughs )
This is a Boeing 737,

00:17:55.707 --> 00:17:58.210 size:88% position:56%
which is the kind of plane
I took to get to California.

00:17:58.243 --> 00:18:03.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Cool.
- And that trip burned
  about this much jet fuel,

00:18:03.581 --> 00:18:07.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is made out of kerosene,
it's a fossil fuel.

00:18:07.418 --> 00:18:10.489 align:start size:69% position:31%
The same amount
of energy in batteries

00:18:10.522 --> 00:18:14.126 align:start size:63% position:38%
would take up
this much space.

00:18:14.159 --> 00:18:16.261 align:start position:0%
Ah, you couldn't even
fit that on there.

00:18:16.294 --> 00:18:17.496 align:start size:81% position:19%
I know, look at the people
compared to the battery.

00:18:17.529 --> 00:18:18.630 align:start size:75% position:25%
- It's gigantic.
- Yeah.

00:18:18.663 --> 00:18:20.332 align:start size:56% position:44%
And this battery
would weigh

00:18:20.365 --> 00:18:22.734 align:start size:69% position:31%
at least 20 times more
than the liquid fuel.

00:18:22.767 --> 00:18:25.137 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
And seven times more
than the airplane itself.

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.672 align:start position:0%
Yeah, and for the jet fuel,
it's going to burn off,

00:18:27.705 --> 00:18:29.307 align:start position:0%
but for the batteries,
they're going to stay

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:30.842 align:start position:0%
