the entire flight.

00:18:30.875 --> 00:18:32.144 align:start size:91% position:9%
Right, it doesn't
get lighter during the flight

00:18:32.177 --> 00:18:33.879 align:start size:81% position:19%
like the liquid fuel does.

00:18:33.912 --> 00:18:36.248 align:start size:59% position:41%
So, the good news
is that batteries
are getting better.

00:18:36.281 --> 00:18:39.151 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- Nice.
- Between 2008 and 2015,

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:41.853 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
the energy density
of batteries nearly doubled,

00:18:41.886 --> 00:18:45.257 align:start size:75% position:25% line:0%
and experts predict
that, in about 30 years,

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:48.927 align:start size:91% position:9%
this plane could fly electric
from New York to Chicago.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.295 align:start size:81% position:19%
Wow.

00:18:50.328 --> 00:18:51.429 align:start size:69% position:31%
But there's a problem.

00:18:51.462 --> 00:18:52.797 align:start size:88% position:13%
Oh, no.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:54.733 align:start size:50% position:50%
80% of emissions
from airplanes

00:18:54.766 --> 00:18:56.568 align:start size:81% position:19%
come from flights that are
longer than that.

00:18:56.601 --> 00:18:57.836 align:start position:0%
Aw, that sucks.

00:18:57.869 --> 00:18:59.404 align:start position:0%
Is there anyone working
on what's going

00:18:59.437 --> 00:19:00.505 size:75% position:38%
to happen in the future?

00:19:00.538 --> 00:19:02.307 align:start position:0%
Is there a super battery
coming up

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:05.277 align:start position:0%
that's going to just change
the way we utilize this energy?

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:07.812 align:start size:81% position:19%
The battery that's
sort of en vogue right now

00:19:07.845 --> 00:19:09.447 size:88% position:56%
is your lithium ion battery.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:10.916
It's what's in electric cars,

00:19:10.949 --> 00:19:13.485 align:start size:72% position:28%
it's what's in
all of our cell phones.

00:19:13.518 --> 00:19:17.322 align:start size:84% position:16%
But some researchers
are looking into completely
different chemistries.

00:19:17.355 --> 00:19:20.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, whether it's electric
planes or hybrids or biofuels,

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:24.596 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's just gonna be some time
before we can engineer away
these emissions.

00:19:24.629 --> 00:19:26.965 align:start size:69% position:31%
And that's because our
industries were built

00:19:26.998 --> 00:19:29.467 align:start size:66% position:34%
on energy dense fuels
that had been

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:32.370 align:start size:69% position:31%
locked underground
for millions of years.

00:19:32.403 --> 00:19:34.372
( imitates plane flying )

00:19:34.405 --> 00:19:35.807
So, is it wrong to fly?

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.842
The short answer,
from my perspective, is no.

00:19:37.875 --> 00:19:39.844 align:start size:78% position:22%
We need mobility.
We have to have mobility.

00:19:39.877 --> 00:19:41.613 align:start size:69% position:31%
But we need to find
ways of doing it

00:19:41.646 --> 00:19:43.949 align:start size:69% position:31%
without emitting
more carbon emissions.

00:19:43.982 --> 00:19:46.418
Joss:
<i> Climate change
 implicates us all</i>

00:19:46.451 --> 00:19:48.720
<i> in a planet-sized injustice.</i>

00:19:48.753 --> 00:19:51.856
<i> If I fly, if I drive,
 if I heat or cool my home,</i>

00:19:51.889 --> 00:19:54.426
<i> if I buy stuff,
 if I eat stuff,</i>

00:19:54.459 --> 00:19:57.562
<i> all of this now has a cost
 that I'm not paying.</i>

00:19:57.595 --> 00:19:59.731
But what's more shameful
than participating

00:19:59.764 --> 00:20:01.766
in a world that was built
for fossil fuels

00:20:01.799 --> 00:20:04.970
is doing nothing
to help bring about
a world that isn't.

00:20:05.003 --> 00:20:07.572
You know, start thinking
about what kinds of decisions

00:20:07.605 --> 00:20:09.474
you're making
for your society around you.

00:20:09.507 --> 00:20:11.576
You know, should we invest
more in trains

00:20:11.609 --> 00:20:15.547
or should we create
more charging infrastructure
for electric cars?

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:18.283
Joss:
<i> The candidates you support
 at a local or national level,</i>

00:20:18.316 --> 00:20:20.652
<i> the infrastructure
that you're willing to pay for.</i>

00:20:20.685 --> 00:20:22.954
I would say we can be judicious
about how we fly.

00:20:22.987 --> 00:20:24.656
